{"abstract":"Atypical hemolytic uremic syndrome (aHUS) is a thrombotic microangiopathy that may lead to organ failure. Dysregulation of the complement system can cause aHUS, and various disease-related variants in the complement regulatory protein CD46 are described. We here report a pediatric patient with aHUS carrying a hitherto unreported homozygous variant in CD46 (NM_172359.3:c.602C>T p.(Ser201Leu)). In our functional analyses, this variant caused complement dysregulation through three separate mechanisms. First, CD46 surface expression on the patient's blood cells was significantly reduced. Second, stably expressing CD46(Ser201Leu) cells bound markedly less to patterns of C3b than CD46 WT cells. Third, the patient predominantly expressed the rare isoforms of CD46 (C dominated) instead of the more common isoforms (BC dominated). Using BC1 and C1 expressing cell lines, we found that the C1 isoform bound markedly less C3b than the BC1 isoform. These results highlight the coexistence of multiple mechanisms that may act synergistically to disrupt CD46 function during aHUS development.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Schack, Vivien","Herlin, Morten Krogh","Pedersen, Henrik","Jensen, Jens Magnus Bernth","Faerch, Mia","Bundgaard, Bettina","Jensen, Rasmus K","Jensen, Uffe Birk","Christensen, Rikke","Andersen, Gregers Rom","Thiel, Steffen","Höllsberg, Per"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-228473"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Höllsberg, Per"],"keyword":["Child","Complement","Complement C3b","Complement System Proteins","Humans","MCP","Mutation","Mutations","Pathway","Protein Isoforms genetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"novel homozygous cd000000000046 variant with c isoform expression affects c000000000003b inactivation in atypical hemolytic uremic syndrome","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/eji.202249838","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-228473","identifier":[{"id":"000847919300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"35987516","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85137328408","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9804674","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-addeae54-c9c0-4b37-91c2-1edcb8bd390a"],"keyword":["Atypical Hemolytic Uremic Syndrome/genetics","C3b","CD46 C-isoform","CD46 variant","COMPLEMENT","Child","Complement C3b","Complement System Proteins","Humans","MCP","MEMBRANE COFACTOR PROTEIN","MUTATIONS","Membrane Cofactor Protein/genetics","Mutation","PATHWAY","Protein Isoforms/genetics","atypical hemolytic syndrome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-99329FBC2D39F882F3C35CBB9B317291"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/331188303/Eur_J_Immunol_2022_Schack_Novel_homozygous_CD46_variant_with_C_isoform_expression_affects_C3b_inactivation_in.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/eji.202249838","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Skou-bygningen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vivien R","key":"schackvivienpau","last":"Schack","locid":"2d96d843-7256-4be1-a674-94ed4d1e629a","name":"Schack, Vivien","name_org":"Schack, Vivien R","orcid":"0000-0002-1365-3938","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten K","key":"herlinmortenkroghpau","last":"Herlin","locid":"22d9393f-f9c2-4fc8-a8e8-4fa48b571a24","name":"Herlin, Morten Krogh","name_org":"Herlin, Morten K","orcid":"0000-0001-7179-4643","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"pedersenhenrikpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"c4aa9b4a-8ebe-4b11-af98-066e754e0a94","name":"Pedersen, Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J Magnus Bernth","key":"jensenjensmagnusbernthpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a67e0021-e11c-47a3-93dd-8f3783ad755a","name":"Jensen, Jens Magnus Bernth","name_org":"Jensen, J Magnus Bernth","orcid":"0000-0002-5004-7822","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mia","key":"faerchmiapau","last":"Faerch","locid":"48c73330-374c-4521-8a40-b21180a1d6b9","name":"Faerch, Mia","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bettina","key":"bundgaardbettinapau","last":"Bundgaard","locid":"ae659a76-be66-4f5a-a560-0f893140d914","name":"Bundgaard, Bettina","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus K","key":"jensenrasmuskpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"f1a46a2f-3f9b-478f-8105-300ddeca70b6","name":"Jensen, Rasmus K","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Uffe B","key":"jensenuffebirkpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"54eb5276-38e5-433b-b654-7f770ddba0ed","name":"Jensen, Uffe Birk","name_org":"Jensen, Uffe B","orcid":"0000-0002-6205-6355","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke","key":"christensenrikkepau","last":"Christensen","locid":"9a145fea-2a3f-4af5-af92-f2dc7f2f9bdb","name":"Christensen, Rikke","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregers R","key":"andersengregersrompau","last":"Andersen","locid":"11cafc34-2c9e-4247-91de-5682cdca052f","name":"Andersen, Gregers Rom","name_org":"Andersen, Gregers R","orcid":"0000-0001-6292-3319","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"thielsteffenpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"beb49137-797f-4a6a-841c-340818b6f472","name":"Thiel, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0002-4817-155X","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"höllsbergperpau","last":"Höllsberg","locid":"cd75c7dd-d33e-41ec-8a0a-9336b0bd7c91","name":"Höllsberg, Per","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35987516"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/eji.202249838","issn":["00142980","15214141"],"issn_org":["00142980"],"issue":"10","journal":"European Journal of Immunology","pages":"1610-1619","publisher":"Wiley-VCH Verlag","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Immunology","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137328408"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-addeae54-c9c0-4b37-91c2-1edcb8bd390a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Novel homozygous CD46 variant with C-isoform expression affects C3b inactivation in atypical hemolytic uremic syndrome","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-228473","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"STUDY QUESTION: Does diet-induced weight loss improve semen parameters, and are these possible improvements maintained with sustained weight loss? SUMMARY ANSWER: An 8-week low-calorie diet-induced weight loss was associated with improved sperm concentration and sperm count, which were maintained after 1 year in men who maintained weight loss. WHAT IS KNOWN ALREADY: Obesity is associated with impaired semen quality. Weight loss improves metabolic health in obesity, but there is a lack of knowledge on the acute and long-term effects of weight loss on semen parameters. STUDY DESIGN, SIZE, DURATION: This is a substudy of men with obesity enrolled in a randomized, controlled, double-blinded trial (the S-LITE trial). The trial was conducted between August 2016 and November 2019. A total of 56 men were included in the study and assigned to an initial 8-week low-calorie diet (800 kcal/day) followed by randomization to 52 weeks of either: placebo and habitual activity (placebo), exercise training and placebo (exercise), the Glucagon Like Peptide 1 (GLP-1) analogue liraglutide and habitual activity (liraglutide) or liraglutide in combination with exercise training (combination). PARTICIPANTS/MATERIALS, SETTING, METHODS: Inclusion criteria were men who delivered semen samples, 18 to 65 years of age, and a body mass index between 32 and 43 kg/m2, but otherwise healthy. The study was carried out at Hvidovre Hospital and at the University of Copenhagen, and the participants were from the Greater Copenhagen Area. We assessed semen parameters and anthropometrics and collected blood samples before (T0), after the 8-week low-calorie dietary intervention (T1), and after 52 weeks (T2). MAIN RESULTS AND THE ROLE OF CHANCE: The men lost on average 16.5 kg (95% CI: 15.2-17.8) body weight during the low-calorie diet, which increased sperm concentration 1.49-fold (95% CI: 1.18-1.88, P < 0.01) and sperm count 1.41-fold (95% CI: 1.07-1.87, P < 0.01). These improvements were maintained for 52 weeks in men who maintained the weight loss, but not in men who regained weight. Semen volume, sperm motility and motile sperm count did not change. LIMITATIONS, REASONS FOR CAUTION: The S-LITE trial was a randomized controlled trial of weight loss maintenance. Analysis of semen was preregistered to explore the effects of weight loss and weight loss maintenance on semen parameters, but definite inferences cannot be made. WIDER IMPLICATIONS OF THE FINDINGS: This study shows that sperm concentration and sperm count were improved after a diet-induced weight loss in men with obesity. Our findings indicate that either or both liraglutide and exercise as weight maintenance strategies may be used to maintain the improvements in sperm concentration and count. STUDY FUNDING/COMPETING INTEREST(S): This work is supported by an excellence grant from the Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF16OC0019968), a Challenge Programme Grant from the Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF18OC0033754) and a grant from Helsefonden. The Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research is an independent research centre at the University of Copenhagen, partially funded by an unrestricted donation from the Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF18CC0034900). Saxenda (liraglutide) and placebo pens were provided by Novo Nordisk. Cambridge Weight Plan diet products for the 8-week low-calorie diet were provided by Cambridge Weight Plan. E.A.: shareholder, employee of ExSeed Health Ltd. Grant Recipient from ExSeed Health Ltd and listed on Patents planned, issued or pending with ExSeed Health Ltd; J.J.H.: consultant for Eli Lilly A/S and Novo Nordisk A/S. Lecture fees for Novo Nordisk A/S. Listed on Patents planned, issued or pending with the University of Copenhagen, Advocacy group for Antag Therapeutics and Bainan Biotech; S.M.: lecture fees for Novo Nordisk A/S. Recipient of Support for attending meetings from Novo Nordisk A/S. Advisory boards of Novo Nordisk A/S; Sanofi Aventis and Merck Sharp & Dohme. S.S.T.: research grant recipient Novo Nordisk. The remaining authors have no conflicts of interest to declare. TRIAL REGISTRATION NUMBER: The trial was approved by the Ethical Committee of the Capital Region of Denmark (H-16027082) and the Danish Medicines Agency (EudraCT Number: 2015-005585-32). ClinicalTrials.gov identifier (NCT number): NCT04122716. TRIAL REGISTRATION DATE: 11 May 2016. DATE OF FIRST PATIENT’S ENROLMENT: August 2016.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Andersen, Emil","Juhl, Christian Rimer","Kjøller, Emma T.","Lundgren, Julie Rehné","Janus, Charlotte","Dehestani, Yasmin","Saupstad, Marte","Ingerslev, Lars Roed","Duun, Olivia M","Jensen, Simon Birk Kjær","Holst, Jens Juul","Stallknecht, Bente","Madsbad, Sten","Torekov, Signe Sørensen","Barrès, Romain"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-478599"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sperm count is increased by diet induced weight loss and maintained by exercise or glp 000000000001 analogue treatment a randomized controlled trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/humrep/deac096","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-478599","identifier":[{"id":"35580859","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9247415","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000796708700001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85133246780","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8e714f37-9727-44b0-a094-31c99f02e037"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B5C32AA18632D0596E0325FB9A1785C2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/313709011/deac096.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/humrep/deac096","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Barrès Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Emil","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"aadc253c-f52c-4938-9879-f51017454fbe","name":"Andersen, Emil","orcid":"0000-0001-6009-2099","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian R","key":"juhlpau","last":"Juhl","locid":"18d8e8fd-21c1-4352-a747-6c0cc9087510","name":"Juhl, Christian Rimer","name_org":"Juhl, Christian R","orcid":"0000-0003-3024-4017","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Emma T.","key":"kjøllerpau","last":"Kjøller","name":"Kjøller, Emma T.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Julie R","key":"lundgrenpau","last":"Lundgren","locid":"88bf4b27-fa5b-4090-a986-cb00acedd3b0","name":"Lundgren, Julie Rehné","name_org":"Lundgren, Julie R","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte","key":"januspau","last":"Janus","locid":"43d27a16-cbc2-4b44-9ebc-858d3083ec5a","name":"Janus, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0001-5111-7047","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yasmin","key":"dehestanipau","last":"Dehestani","name":"Dehestani, Yasmin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marte","key":"saupstadpau","last":"Saupstad","locid":"191898a4-b1ee-4911-9a19-6515fe952e98","name":"Saupstad, Marte","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars R","key":"ingerslevpau","last":"Ingerslev","locid":"26f3d9d2-f555-4a5b-9fda-25333d1838ed","name":"Ingerslev, Lars Roed","name_org":"Ingerslev, Lars R","orcid":"0000-0002-4164-7690","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Olivia M","key":"duunpau","last":"Duun","name":"Duun, Olivia M","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Simon B K","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"9edd5734-2279-4744-b174-f70c08e9ad82","name":"Jensen, Simon Birk Kjær","name_org":"Jensen, Simon B K","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens J","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","name_org":"Holst, Jens J","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bente M","key":"stallknechtpau","last":"Stallknecht","locid":"eddf86eb-44d6-44ca-985b-79a29dd3cec7","name":"Stallknecht, Bente","name_org":"Stallknecht, Bente M","orcid":"0000-0003-3117-0451","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Signe S","key":"torekovpau","last":"Torekov","locid":"c1d71a61-ee09-4c29-ae48-7520707a73be","name":"Torekov, Signe Sørensen","name_org":"Torekov, Signe S","orcid":"0000-0001-6779-0252","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Romain","key":"barrèspau","last":"Barrès","locid":"19b8079b-9b9e-4067-adb0-a66ab70f184f","name":"Barrès, Romain","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-519X","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35580859"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/humrep/deac096","issn":["02681161","14602350"],"issn_org":["02681161"],"issue":"7","journal":"Human Reproduction","pages":"1414-1422","status":"p","title":"Human Reproduction","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133246780"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8e714f37-9727-44b0-a094-31c99f02e037"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Sperm count is increased by diet-induced weight loss and maintained by exercise or GLP-1 analogue treatment : a randomized controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-478599","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease (CMT) is a heterogeneous group of hereditary polyneuropathies. Variants in more than 80 different genes have been associated with the disorder. In recent years, the introduction of next generation sequencing (NGS) techniques have completely changed the genetic diagnostic approach from the analysis of a handful of genes to the analysis of all genes associated with CMT in a single run. In this study we describe the CMT diagnostics in Denmark in 1992-2012, prior to the implementation of NGS, by combining laboratory- and national registry data. We investigate the effect of implementing a targeted NGS approach of 63 genes associated with CMT in the diagnostic laboratory setting. This was performed by analyzing a cohort of 195 samples from patients previously analyzed by Sanger sequencing and quantitative analysis for the common causes of CMT without reaching a molecular diagnosis. A total of 1442 CMT analyses were performed in Denmark in the period 1992-2012; a disease-causing variant was detected in 21.6% of the cases. Interestingly, the diagnosis was genetically confirmed in significantly more women than men; 25.9% compared to18.5%. In our study cohort, we found a 5.6% increase in the diagnostic yield with the introduction of a targeted NGS approach.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Væth, Signe","Christensen, Rikke","Dunø, Morten","Lildballe, Dorte Launholt","Thorsen, Kasper","Vissing, John","Svenstrup, Kirsten","Hertz, Jens Michael","Andersen, Henning","Jensen, Uffe Birk"],"cuid":["S03-094.35-017404"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Vaeth, Signe"],"keyword":["Charcot Marie Tooth disease","Denmark","Facilities and Services Utilization","Genetic Testing methods","Genetic epidemiology","High Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing methods","Humans","Massively parallel sequencing","Registries","Sequence Analysis DNA methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic analysis of charcot marie tooth disease in denmark and the implementation of a next generation sequencing platform","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/251255338/Genetic_analysis_of_Charcot_Marie_Tooth_disease_in_Denmark_and_the_implementation_of_a.PDF","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We are grateful to the following for assistance in medical records retrieval: Dea Svaneby, Dept. of Clinical Genetics, Vejle, Suzanne Lindquist, Dept. of Clinical Genetics, Rigshospitalet, Lisbeth Landschoff, Dept. of Neurology, Glostrup, Lise Korbo, Dept. of Neurology, Bispebjerg, Birgitte Forsom Sandal, Dept. of Neurology, Holstebro, and the administrative staff at the Departments of Neurology in Roskilde and Hillerød and the Departments of Pediatrics in Næstved and Hvidovre. From the Dept. of Clinical Genetics, Aarhus, we wish to thank Jan Hansen and Inger Junker for the retrieval of genetic analysis data, and Klaus Riege Cookiemayn Nielsen and Christina Strande Sønderskov for the preparation of DNA and Sanger sequencing of samples. We also wish to thank Michael Væth from The Department of Public Health, Section for Biostatistics at Aarhus University for technical assistance in the management of register data. This work has been supported by a grant from Innovation Fund Denmark ( 037-2010-1 ), Aarhus University Hospital and Aarhus University , and was also funded by Fonden til Lægevidenskabens Fremme , Vanførefonden , Torben og Alice Frimodts Fond , Aase og Einar Danielsens Fond , Civilingeniør Frode V . Nyegaard og hustrus Fond and Familien Hede Nielsens Fond . Appendix A"],"id":"S03-094.35-017404","identifier":[{"id":"85045848193","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29653220","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-40cc2985-ca27-4206-8714-229ccf72f436","ku-d8647825-8778-4144-b118-126b9cecf4e1","sdu-4c128e51-d004-4d6b-a57a-e1f0489fd1c0"],"keyword":["Charcot-Marie-Tooth Disease","Charcot-Marie-Tooth Disease/diagnosis","Denmark","Facilities and Services Utilization","Genetic Testing/methods","Genetic epidemiology","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing/methods","Humans","Massively parallel sequencing","Registries","Sequence Analysis, DNA/methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-DF8082DDC5C07981BA6AA8B707E3AFA0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/251255338/Genetic_analysis_of_Charcot_Marie_Tooth_disease_in_Denmark_and_the_implementation_of_a.PDF","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/142979888/G_SRPI92.PDF","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department for Clinical Genetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hos